A naive clone has no WeakMap:<pre><code>function clone(v) {
  if (typeof v !== "object" || v === null) return v
  const out = {}
  for (const k of Object.keys(v)) out[k] = clone(v[k])
  return out
}
const a = {}
a.me = a
clone(a)</code></pre>What happens?

Someone adds a WeakMap but registers the copy <b>after</b> filling it:<pre><code>const out = {}
for (const k of Object.keys(v)) out[k] = clone(v[k], seen)
seen.set(v, out)
return out</code></pre>Does this fix the circular case <code>a.me = a</code>?

