problems.solution:
function groupBy(array, key) {
  const getLabel = typeof key === 'function'
    ? key
    : (item) => (item == null ? undefined : item[key]);
  const result = Object.create(null);
  array.forEach((item, index) => {
    const label = getLabel(item, index);
    if (!(label in result)) result[label] = [];
    result[label].push(item);
  });
  return result;
}

think.q:
How many times is the callback called, and what is returned?<pre><code>let calls = 0
const r = [1, 2, 3].reduce((a, b) =&gt; { calls++; return a + b })
console.log(calls, r)</code></pre>

Someone writes <code>myMap</code> like this:<pre><code>function myMap(arr, fn) {
  const out = []
  for (const x of arr) out.push(fn(x))
  return out
}</code></pre>What does <code>myMap(["a", "b"], (x, i) =&gt; i)</code> return?

